# Aadal Archive — Design System Palette (locked)

Use this palette for all UI work. Do not introduce red, maroon, burgundy, crimson, vermilion, wine, or reddish-brown.

## Core colors

| Role | Hex | Use |
|------|-----|-----|
| Soft black | `#0D1012` | Deepest background |
| Deep charcoal | `#15161A` | App / page background |
| Charcoal surface | `#1C1E24` | Panels, forms |
| Elevated charcoal | `#24262B` | Elevated surfaces |
| Antique gold | `#E5A93C` | Primary actions, active states |
| Light gold | `#F0C56A` | Soft gold highlights |
| Bronze gold | `#A8752B` | Borders, labels |
| Deep bronze | `#6E4A1C` | Engraved depth |
| Warm ivory | `#F4EBDD` | Primary text |
| Soft beige | `#D8C6A7` | Secondary text |
| Muted teal | `#0E627A` | Secondary accent |
| Deep teal | `#16495A` | Shadow / veil |
| Blue teal | `#1C7B8F` | Soft light accents |
| Muted orange | `#F38222` | Sparse tertiary (~3%) |
| Dark orange | `#A94D12` | Sparse tertiary depth |
| Neutral grey | `#77736D` | Quiet meta text |

Balance ≈ 55% charcoal/black · 20% ivory/beige · 15% gold/bronze · 7% teal · 3% orange.

## Iconography

Use `HeritageIcons` from `src/components/heritage/HeritageIcons.tsx` for post-login UI — mudra, salangai, temple bell, doorway motifs. Never use emoji for actions.

## Decsheets

Temple architecture frames content (5–10%). Prefer SVG/CSS ornaments and existing `/public/temple/clean/` assets. Content imagery first.
